<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Load Columns</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body style="width: 300px">
    <h3>Load Columns</h3>
    <p>
        Reads a small sample of the CSV through the database connection to find its columns.
    </p>
    <p>
        If the first row contains column names, they are used. Otherwise the columns are named
        <code>COLUMN_1</code>, <code>COLUMN_2</code>, and so on. The sample also identifies
        columns whose values appear numeric.
    </p>
    <p>
        The source file is read only and is not changed.
    </p>
</body>
</html>
